  "Number": 7,
  "Question": "An error of \\(0.02''\\) is made in the measurement of a line \\(10''\\) long, while an error of only \\(0.2''\\) is made in a measurement of a line \\(100''\\) long. In comparison with the relative error of the first measurement, the relative error of the second measurement is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Greater by \\(0.18\\)",
    "B": "The same",
    "C": "Less",
    "D": "\\(10\\) times as great",
    "E": "Correctly described by both \\((A)\\) and \\((D)\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Relative error is the size of the measurement error divided by the actual length, with both expressed in the same units. The two relative errors are\n\\[\n\\frac{0.02}{10}=0.002,\n\\qquad\n\\frac{0.2}{100}=0.002.\n\\]\nThey are equal, so the answer is choice B.",
